{"archetypes":[{"name":"ci-gate","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The core change is a subtle two-phase GitHub required-check gate with stale-head and registration-race failure modes.","prompt_body":"Examine the two-phase required-check registration and watch flow in scripts/design-log-publish.sh. Verify the pushed-head binding, probe budget, sleep behavior, gh exit-code handling, jq parsing, and no-watch timeout behavior cannot merge on stale or absent CI state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"gh-stub","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The regression value depends on the PATH-injected gh stub accurately modeling GitHub behavior rather than making tests pass by construction.","prompt_body":"Review scripts/test-design-log-publish.sh as a simulation of GitHub and git state. Check whether pr checks --json, pr checks --watch, pr view headRefOid, branch OID derivation, mismatch knobs, and log assertions faithfully exercise the production merge gate without masking failures. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"stdout-contract","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"These scripts have machine-readable stdout contracts, and the diff adds jq, gh, cat, and stderr-capture paths that could leak non-contract output.","prompt_body":"Audit shell contract hygiene for scripts that emit KEY=value lines and larch quiet streams. Look for accidental stdout leakage from jq, gh diagnostics, cat or tee changes, helper failures, warnings, or captured stderr replay that would corrupt machine-readable consumers. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-state","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Re-enabling the flush changes cross-script lifecycle semantics for result env fields, rename gating, summaries, and recovery branches.","prompt_body":"Trace the /design publish lifecycle across skills/design/scripts/design-publish.sh, scripts/design-log-publish.sh, their tests, and the updated docs. Verify PUBLISH_OK, PR_NUMBER, PR_URL, RECOVERY_BRANCH, post-publish summary rendering, issue rename gating, and failure exits remain consistent across callers and documented contracts. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"temp-cleanup","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds temporary files and altered cleanup paths in shell scripts where early returns and set -e interactions often cause regressions.","prompt_body":"Inspect temporary-file creation, cleanup, and error paths introduced or changed in the shell scripts. Pay special attention to mktemp failures, early returns, set -e boundaries, stale capture files, worktree removal, recovery branch emission, and plan-review collector stderr temp handling. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
